{"n":65,"verses":[{"k":1,"w":[["يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا","yaaayyuhaa"],["ٱلنَّبِىُّ","l-nabiyu"],["إِذَا","idhaa"],["طَلَّقْتُمُ","tallaqtumu"],["ٱلنِّسَآءَ","l-nisaaa"],["فَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ","fatalliqoohunna"],["لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ","li'iddatihinna"],["وَأَحْصُوا۟","wa-ahsoo"],["ٱلْعِدَّةَ ۖ","l-'idata"],["وَٱتَّقُوا۟","wa-ittaqoo"],["ٱللَّهَ","l-laha"],["رَبَّكُمْ ۖ","rabbakum"],["لَا","laa"],["تُخْرِجُوهُنَّ","tukh'rijoohunna"],["مِنۢ","min"],["بُيُوتِهِنَّ","buyootihinna"],["وَلَا","walaa"],["يَخْرُجْنَ","yakhruj'na"],["إِلَّآ","illaa"],["أَن","an"],["يَأْتِينَ","yateena"],["بِفَـٰحِشَةٍۢ","bifaahishatin"],["مُّبَيِّنَةٍۢ ۚ","mubayyinatin"],["وَتِلْكَ","watil'ka"],["حُدُودُ","hudoodu"],["ٱللَّهِ ۚ","l-lahi"],["وَمَن","waman"],["يَتَعَدَّ","yata'adda"],["حُدُودَ","hudooda"],["ٱللَّهِ","l-lahi"],["فَقَدْ","faqad"],["ظَلَمَ","zalama"],["نَفْسَهُۥ ۚ","nafsahu"],["لَا","laa"],["تَدْرِى","tadree"],["لَعَلَّ","la'alla"],["ٱللَّهَ","l-laha"],["يُحْدِثُ","yuh'dithu"],["بَعْدَ","ba'da"],["ذَٰلِكَ","dhaalika"],["أَمْرًۭا","amran"]],"en":"O Prophet, when you [Muslims] divorce women, divorce them for [the commencement of] their waiting period and keep count of the waiting period, and fear Allah, your Lord. Do not turn them out of their [husbands'] houses, nor should they [themselves] leave [during that period] unless they are committing a clear immorality. And those are the limits [set by] Allah. And whoever transgresses the limits of Allah has certainly wronged himself. You know not; perhaps Allah will bring about after that a [different] matter.","t":{"6":[[850,3240],[3250,4640],[4650,5190],[5200,6580],[6590,9070],[9080,11490],[11500,13710],[13720,14580],[14590,16550],[18500,19320],[19330,20100],[20110,21900],[22700,23060],[23070,25460],[25470,26430],[26440,28490],[28500,29170],[29180,30300],[30310,32250],[32260,33470],[33480,34610],[34620,37020],[37030,41180],[41190,42010],[42020,43210],[43220,45900],[46600,47560],[47570,48730],[48740,49780],[49790,50770],[50780,51420],[51430,52360],[523